# ai.wing — Changelog

Structural changes, feature additions and component creations for the
GCI Authorized Retailer landing site.

Format: newest entry at the top. Each entry records what changed and why.

---

## [3.1.0] — Mobile responsiveness, GitHub, Vercel

### Responsive audit

Measured at 320 / 360 / 375 / 414 / 540 / 768 / 900 / 1024 px rather than eyed,
checking document width against viewport, every element's box, computed font
sizes and tap-target heights.

**No horizontal overflow at any width**, before or after. The elements flagged
as extending past the viewport are all deliberately clipped decoration — the
105%-scaled hero photograph, the marquee track, the medallion orbits.

Four real problems, all fixed:

| Problem | Was | Now |
|---|---|---|
| H1 at 320px | 38px over 5 lines | 31px over 3 lines |
| Offer medallion at 320px | 256px — 80% of the screen | 192px, stepped up by breakpoint |
| Smallest text | 9px | 10px |
| Footer tap targets | 17px tall | 44px |

The headings were the root cause: every `clamp()` had a floor too high for a
small screen, so the `vw` term never engaged and the minimum always won. Floors
lowered and the `vw` terms raised across all headings, hero copy and the
medallion, so type now genuinely scales down rather than clamping flat.

Medallion, orbits and glow now step through breakpoints together
(`12rem → 16rem → 18rem → clamp`), so the whole assembly including its rings
fits inside a 320px screen with margin to spare.

### Touch behaviour

**Tilt and magnetic effects are now gated behind `(hover: hover) and
(pointer: fine)`.** Touch screens synthesise a `mousemove` on tap but never
fire `mouseleave`, so a tapped card stayed stuck mid-tilt. New
`useFinePointer()` hook for the React build, an equivalent media query check in
the static build. It starts false so server and client render agree.

### Repository

Pushed to `github.com/PavithraEbbali/gci` on `main`. 67 files, no
`node_modules`, images 1.2 MB total.

- `.gitignore` covers `node_modules`, `.next`, the generated `build/*.mjs`
  bundles and local QA scratch files
- `README.md` documents both builds, the content architecture, the omitted
  service lines and the pre-launch placeholders
- `playwright` removed from devDependencies — it was only ever a QA tool

### Vercel

Auto-detected as a Next.js app at the repository root; no `vercel.json` needed.
Clean production build: 12 routes, all static, 181 kB first load.

**One environment variable must be set** or social link previews resolve against
localhost: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`. Documented in `.env.example` and the README.

---

## [3.0.0] — Static HTML build

The whole site now also exists as plain HTML, CSS and vanilla JavaScript in
`html/`. No React, no Node server, no build step to run it — `index.html`
opens straight off the filesystem.

### Approach

Not a hand transcription. The markup is **generated from the same
`lib/content.ts` the Next app reads**, via esbuild bundles of the content and
legal modules, so the two builds cannot drift apart. The stylesheet is compiled
by Tailwind from the same `@theme` token block against the generated HTML, so
the class names and resulting CSS are the same ones the app uses.

`npm run build:html` runs the whole pipeline: bundle content, generate pages,
compile CSS, copy JS and images.

### What was ported, and how

| Effect | Replacement |
|---|---|
| Lenis smooth scroll | Lenis from CDN, same settings, guarded so a failed load degrades to native scrolling |
| Hero entrance | Already CSS keyframes — copied as-is |
| Scroll reveals, stagger grids | IntersectionObserver toggling `.is-in`, CSS transitions carry the motion |
| Clip-path section wipes | Same mechanism, on `clip-path` |
| Parallax | Scroll handler batched into one rAF tick |
| SVG speed-path draw | `getTotalLength()` feeding a dash-offset transition |
| Magnetic buttons | Pointer tracking with eased follow; label still parallaxes at 42% |
| 3D card tilt | Pointer tracking, still capped at 7° |
| Aurora canvas | Ported verbatim — it was already vanilla canvas |
| Marquee, medallion orbits and glow | Already pure CSS |
| ZIP checker, FAQ accordion, mobile menu, scroll-spy | Plain event handlers |

### Verified against the running Next app

Both served side by side and compared:

- Section order identical; 7 images, 0 broken, in both
- Page height 14,835 vs 14,903 px — within 0.5%
- Zero JS errors and zero console errors in both
- Hero renders pixel-identical, including medallion, orbits, glow and photo
- ZIP checker: all three states correct
- Reveals 47/51 fired, wipes 8/8, stagger grids 6/6, speed-path 1/1
- FAQ stays single-open and moves the `aria-expanded` state correctly
- Tilt measured at `rotateX(3.5deg) rotateY(-4.22deg)`, magnetic label at 42%
  of body travel — matching the React implementation
- Legal pages: 8 cross-links and 8 footer links, CSS loaded, no errors
- `file://` verified: CSS, canvas, medallion and images all work by
  double-clicking, with no errors

Playwright's synthetic pointer does not trigger tilt or magnetic in headless
for **either** build, so that was confirmed as a harness artifact rather than a
regression by dispatching the events directly.

