## [2.0.1] — Final verification pass

Caught by re-running the constraint sweep and a DOM audit against the built
site, after an unrelated process took port 3000 and the dev server had to be
moved to **3010** (`.claude/launch.json` updated).

- **`RevealText` accent join produced one merged word.** The gap between the
  base phrase and the accent phrase was a CSS-width spacer (`w-[0.3em]`), which
  renders visually but does not exist in the text layer — so the Why GCI
  heading read "networkinvestment" to assistive tech, to copied text and to
  search engines. Replaced with a real non-breaking space emitted by the last
  base word; the spacer element is gone.
- **Two Why GCI card rewrites had silently not applied** in an earlier batch
  (quote-escaping mismatch meant the replace was a no-op and nothing warned).
  The "#1" card now reads "Independently rated fastest in Alaska" with the
  rewritten body, matching the rest of the section's register.

### Verified on the built site

- Section order: top → offers → fiber → bundles → mobile → phone → fine-print
  → why-gci → faq. No `#tv` or `#cable` section exists.
- Constraint sweep, all false: support routing, "ordering channel", competitor
  bashing, date stamps, broadband-label links, "official site" FAQ, GCI's own
  support number, and any trace of the old placeholder brand name.
- Only two call-to-action label strings exist site-wide: "Call to order" and
  the header/footer "Call (855) 555-0142". Zero raw phone numbers used as
  interactive labels inside `<main>`.
- Hero carries the ZIP checker, the "Call to order" button, the featured
  iPhone 18 Pro offer, and no "or dial" line.
- Eight legal links in the footer.
- `tsc --noEmit` clean; `next build` clean, 12/12 routes static, 173 kB first
  load.

---

## [2.0.0] — Light-theme rebuild, GCI branding, offers rail, new footer

### Theme: dark → light, vibrant

- The site now reads white-dominant, the way gci.com does. `globals.css`
  replaces the dark canvases with `.canvas-hero`, `.canvas-white`,
  `.canvas-tint` (#f2f5fa) and two dark accents kept for the footer and the
  closing CTA band. Brand red carries action, glacier blue carries energy.
- **Palette is locked to the scraped GCI tokens.** A computed-style audit was
  run across every element on the rendered page, checking `color`,
  `background-color` and all four border colours against the allowed list.
  Result: zero off-palette values in the application DOM. (One `#757575`
  appears inside the Next.js dev-overlay shadow root, which does not ship.)
- Hero backdrop rewritten: `BlackHole.tsx` (dark void, lensed starfield) →
  `AuroraField.tsx`, a light refracting lens with drifting particles and
  aurora ribbons, composited with normal alpha because additive blending
  washes to white on a light canvas.

### Navbar seam

- The header previously faded from transparent over a dark hero, which left a
  visible divider line where the utility bar met the hero canvas, and rendered
  the white wordmark invisible against the white body behind it.
- Replaced with gci.com's own structure: a charcoal (`#303139`) utility bar
  that scrolls away, and a header that is solid white from first paint with a
  shadow that appears on scroll. The hero no longer needs the negative-margin
  pull-up, so the seam is gone by construction.

### Branding

- `site.brandName` is now **GCI** with `brandSuffix: 'Authorized Retailer'`.
  The former placeholder name is removed from every surface — header, footer,
  hero, metadata and all eight legal pages (verified: zero occurrences in
  source or rendered output).
- `lib/legal.ts` was rewritten so the policies read in the first person
  ("we", "this site") rather than naming a separate company, which would have
  been nonsensical once the brand became GCI.
- The persistent "Independent Authorized Retailer of GCI." disclosure bar
  stays at the top of every page, and the footer carries the full trademark
  attribution to GCI Communication Corp.

### Current offers

- New `specialOffers` array in `lib/content.ts`, transcribed from gci.com:
  iPhone 18 Pro on us, free unlimited mobile for a year, iPhone 17 Pro for $0,
  up to $1,000 off Galaxy S26, iPhone 17e on us, $350 off iPad Air (M4), 30%
  off three or more accessories.
- The featured offer (iPhone 18 Pro) now occupies the hero's right-hand card.
- New `components/sections/Offers.tsx` renders the full promotions rail: a
  large red lead card with qualifying points, plus a six-card grid. Sits
  directly after the hero, and is linked from the nav as "Deals".

### Copy — professional rewrite

Every heading and standfirst called out for revision was rewritten:

| Section | Now reads |
|---|---|
| Hero | "Alaska's fastest internet, built on the Fiber+ network." |
| Fiber+ | "Choose the speed tier that fits your household" |
| Bundles | "Internet and mobile on a single bill" |
| Mobile | "Nationwide coverage on Alaska's fastest 5G network" |
| Phone | "Reliable landline service with unlimited calling" |
| Fine print | "Every charge, shown side by side" |
| Why GCI | "Four decades of network investment in Alaska" |
| CTA band | "Confirm what is available at your address" |
| FAQ | "Frequently asked questions" |

Supporting paragraphs were rewritten in the same register — declarative,
specific, no folksy asides.

### Hero

- Removed the "or dial (855) 555-0142" secondary line. The prominent
  "Call to order" button is retained, since the brief's hard constraint
  requires the hero to carry both a ZIP checker and a call button.

### Plan cards

- The "Call to order" button moved to the **bottom** of every card, with
  `mt-auto` pinning it to the card's lower edge so every CTA in a row sits on
  a common baseline regardless of how many feature bullets a plan carries.

### Footer — rebuilt on the reference layout

- Four-column top band: brand and tagline, SHOP column, LEARN column, and a
  "Talk to a human" column with the phone number set large, plus hours and
  location.
- Full **OFFER DETAILS & REQUIRED DISCLOSURES** block driven by
  `footerDisclosures` in `lib/content.ts` — ten disclosure paragraphs covering
  internet, data allowances, bundles, mobile, roaming, streaming device, home
  phone, Atmos Rewards, equipment and general terms. Rendered in two columns
  on desktop.
- Bottom bar carries all eight legal pages, a compliance contact line and the
  trademark copyright.
- Deliberately **omitted** the reference site's "Pricing current as of
  [date]" line, since the brief prohibits date stamps.

### Other fixes

- `RevealText` word masks now reserve `0.2em` below the baseline so descenders
  are not clipped in headlines.
- Accent gradients constrained to the blue ramp (`#007aa1 → #00a9e0`); the
  previous blue→red gradient passed through a muddy grey mid-tone.
- Anchor targets get `scroll-margin-top` so the sticky header never covers a
  section heading after an in-page jump.

