## [1.0.1] — QA pass

Fixes found by rendering the built site in a real browser at 1440px and 390px.

### Correctness

- **Hero entrance moved from JS to CSS.** The `<h1>` is the LCP element and was
  shipping at `opacity: 0` behind a Framer Motion `animate`, so it stayed blank
  anywhere the animation loop was throttled and cost LCP unnecessarily. It now
  uses `@keyframes rise-in` with `animation-fill-mode: backwards`, so the
  resting state is visible and the hidden state exists only while the animation
  is pending. Below-the-fold scroll reveals stay on Framer Motion, which is what
  they are for.
- **Header now overlays the hero.** The sticky header sat *above* the hero in
  flow, leaving a white band across the top and rendering the white wordmark
  invisible against it. The hero is pulled up under the header with a matching
  negative margin and compensating padding.
- **FAQ sticky column restored.** The section carried `overflow-hidden`, which
  gave the sticky intro column a scrolling ancestor that never scrolls, so it
  silently stopped sticking. Removed — nothing in that section overflows.
- **Corrected a date claim.** "Forty years" understated GCI's history; gci.com
  dates the company to 1979. Copy now anchors on the year, and the fiber-backbone
  card reads "more than four decades".
- **Removed two raw phone numbers used as interactive labels inside `<main>`.**
  The hero's secondary line is now plain text, and the ZIP success CTA reads
  "Call to order". Raw numbers remain only in the header, mobile menu and footer.

### Layout and polish

- Speed readouts split the numeral from the unit (`splitSpeed()`), so
  "500 Mbps" no longer wraps to two lines in a four-across grid.
- Plan-card name and tagline reserve fixed heights, so the speed, price and CTA
  rows line up across cards even when one plan name wraps.
- Badge slot is a fixed `h-7` whether or not a badge is present, removing a 3px
  vertical offset between the featured card and its neighbours.
- Scroll-spy clears the nav highlight once no service section owns the viewport,
  instead of leaving the last one lit through the FAQ and footer.
- Black-hole backdrop softened — hairline photon ring, wider and fainter bloom,
  smaller radius — so it reads as atmosphere rather than a drawn circle. On
  phones the void sits higher so it no longer sits behind the ZIP field.
- Promo pill label no longer breaks across two lines on narrow screens.
- Frosted header raised to 93% opacity so body copy does not read through it.

### Verified

- `tsc --noEmit` clean; `next build` clean, 12/12 routes static.
- Rendered and reviewed at 1440×900 and 390×844: hero, all four service
  sections, fine-print grid, Why GCI, FAQ, footer, mobile menu, ZIP checker
  success state, and a legal page.
- Constraint sweep run against the live DOM: no support-routing copy, no
  broadband-label links, no date stamps, no competitor bashing, no TV or cable
  section, no "official site" FAQ, every plan CTA reads "Call to order".

