## [1.0.0] — Initial build

### Research & source of truth

- **Scraped `https://www.gci.com` design-token layer** to extract the official
  brand palette. Resolved the `--colors-colors-*` custom properties from GCI's
  live stylesheet rather than eyeballing screenshots:
  - `#b71234` brand red (hover `#9b0f2c`, pressed `#800d24`)
  - `#042046` midnight blue · `#073473` link midnight
  - `#00a9e0` glacier blue · `#31ccff` glacier bright · `#007aa1` glacier deep
  - `#23252a` darkest · `#303139` dark · `#5e636e` mid · `#c6c9d2` light
  - `#e1e4ea` border · `#f2f5fa` lightest
- **Typography audit**: GCI ships Gotham (Light/Book/Medium/Bold). Paired
  Montserrat (closest freely-licensable geometric sans) for display with Inter
  for body copy.
- **Service-line audit** against gci.com. Findings drove which sections exist:

  | Line | Finding | Action |
  |---|---|---|
  | Fiber+ Internet | 4 live tiers | Built |
  | Cable | No separate cable lineup — one residential internet lineup runs over the hybrid Fiber+ build | **Omitted** |
  | Bundles (GCI+) | 4 live bundles | Built |
  | TV | `/tv` redirects to homepage; `/tv/plans` and `/yukon-tv` return 404 | **Omitted entirely** |
  | Mobile | 4 live plans | Built |
  | Home Phone | 3 live plans | Built |

- All plan data (prices, speeds, caps, overage increments, fees, promo terms)
  transcribed from GCI's own plan pages and broadband disclosures.

### Architecture

- **`lib/content.ts` — single source of truth.** Every price, speed, plan name,
  feature bullet, fee row, FAQ and nav link originates here. No component
  hard-codes content. Exposes `PlanItem`, `ServiceSection`, `FinePrintRow`,
  `FeatureItem`, `FaqItem` plus helpers `formatSpeed()`, `ctaLabel()` and
  `plansFor()`.
  - `ctaLabel()` enforces the CTA rule: `"Call to order"` when a plan has a
    published price, `"Call for pricing"` when it does not.
  - `serviceSections` drives the page — adding or removing a line there adds or
    removes a whole section with no component changes.
- **`lib/legal.ts`** — structured content for the eight required legal pages.
- Strict-frontend throughout: no API routes, no database, no server actions.
  The ZIP checker evaluates Alaska ZIP prefixes in the browser and stores
  nothing.

### Components created

**Providers**
- `components/providers/LenisProvider.tsx` — Lenis smooth scrolling, anchor
  links routed through it, fully disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion`.

**UI primitives**
- `components/ui/PriceLockup.tsx` — universal `<PriceLockup plan={plan} />`.
  Raised dollar sign, 2.5–3.5rem integer, muted raised cents, optional struck
  regular price, tabular numerals, single clean screen-reader utterance.
  Degrades to "Custom pricing" when no price is published.
- `components/ui/MagneticButton.tsx` — magnetic cursor-follow CTA with spring
  return; label parallaxes at 42% of body travel. Five variants, three sizes.
- `components/ui/TiltCard.tsx` — 3D tilt on mouse-move for plan cards, capped
  at 7° so pricing stays legible, with a cursor-tracked specular highlight.
- `components/ui/Reveal.tsx` — `RevealText` (per-word clip-mask headline
  reveal), `Reveal` (fade + lift), `StaggerGrid` / `StaggerItem`.
- `components/ui/Motion.tsx` — `Parallax` (scroll-linked depth drift),
  `SectionWipe` (clip-path wipe between service sections), `Marquee`
  (seamless infinite ticker, pauses on hover, edge-masked), `SpeedPath`
  (SVG path-draw visualising the speed tiers).
- `components/ui/BlackHole.tsx` — canvas deep-space hero backdrop: lensed
  starfield, breathing photon ring, aurora ribbons in glacier blue and brand
  red. DPR capped at 1.5, rAF suspended via IntersectionObserver when
  off-screen, disabled entirely under reduced-motion.

**Sections**
- `components/sections/Header.tsx` — persistent top disclosure bar plus sticky
  header that transitions transparent → frosted on scroll, with scroll-spy
  anchor nav (shared `layoutId` pill) and a call CTA. Exports `PhoneGlyph`.
- `components/sections/Hero.tsx` — black-hole backdrop, live-promo pill,
  gradient headline, **both** the ZIP availability checker **and** a prominent
  "Call to order" button, stat strip, promo card, speed ticker.
- `components/sections/PlanSection.tsx` — one generic section rendering any
  service line from `content.ts`; tilt plan cards, `PriceLockup`, policy chips.
- `components/sections/FinePrintGrid.tsx` — trust marquee plus the inclusions
  and fees grid; real `<table>` on desktop, per-service stacks on mobile.
- `components/sections/WhyGci.tsx` — staggered feature grid over parallax glow
  plates, closing CTA band.
- `components/sections/Faq.tsx` — accordion with sticky intro column, full
  `aria-expanded` / `aria-controls` wiring.
- `components/sections/Footer.tsx` — dark premium footer with reseller
  disclosure and all eight legal links.

**Routes**
- `app/page.tsx` — composes the fixed section order.
- `app/legal/[slug]/page.tsx` — statically generated legal pages with a sticky
  cross-index of all eight.
- `app/globals.css` — GCI tokens as a Tailwind v4 `@theme`, layout primitives,
  atmosphere utilities, marquee keyframes, reduced-motion overrides.

### Compliance with the negative constraints

- No support-routing copy anywhere — nothing tells a user to contact GCI for
  billing, outages or support.
- Hero carries both the ZIP checker and a prominent call button.
- Every plan-card and section CTA reads "Call to order"; raw phone numbers
  appear only in the header, footer and as literal contact information.
- No competitor bashing; no "ordering channel" language.
- No section exists for a service GCI does not sell; no empty placeholders.
- No links to official Broadband Facts labels.
- No "Pricing observed [date]" stamps.
- No FAQ about official-site status or retailer legal structure.

### Notes for the next editor

- `site.phoneDisplay` / `site.phoneHref` in `lib/content.ts` hold a placeholder
  in the reserved 555-01xx fictional range. **Replace both before launch.**
- To change any price: edit `lib/content.ts` only.
